      <tei:div type="colophon" subtype="introduction">
        <tei:p>“Éikh Mishkenai Elyōn” is the first reshut offered before Nishmat at the outset of Shaḥarit (concluding the Zemirot). It is the third reshut among the reshuyot in the Old Sefaradi Tiqun for Shabbat Ḥazon — the final shabbat before 9 Av.</tei:p>
        <tei:p>The color red indicates text found in the oldest manuscripts and which is necessary for the completion of the acrostic, but which is not found in many printings.</tei:p>
      </tei:div>
      <j:endConditional target="#osp_68328_introduction"/>
